# notes-tex/030-scaling-study/Makefile
# [[experiments.030-solid-growth-multi.scripts.scaling_readout_030]]
# https://github.com/Mjvolk3/torchcell/tree/main/notes-tex/030-scaling-study/Makefile
#
# The scaling study on the 030 per-entry build: the grid queued on Delta, what it logs,
# how it is read, what each fit can support, and the planned figures. The forms and the
# fitting recipe are the scaling-laws explainer's (notes-tex/modeling/scaling-laws, on the
# docs/scaling-laws branch); this document is the study against them. No Zotero
# collection: the three scaling papers are named by mirror key in prose, as the explainer
# does, so references.bib is empty on purpose.
#
# Tables are written by experiments/030-solid-growth-multi/scripts/scaling_grid_table_030.py
# (run from the repo root with PYTHONPATH=$PWD). The four planned figures are draw.io
# sources generated by notes/assets/drawio/030-scaling-study.gen.py; `make figures`
# exports them (DRAWIO=<binary> on Linux, see [[drawio-headless-export-gilahyper]]).
# The results figure itself is written by scaling_readout_030.py once the grid has run;
# until then its slot is a placeholder.

include ../common/Makefile.common
